1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
How to sew a sewing machine

2
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:04,000
How to sew a sewing machine

3
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:06,000
How to sew a sewing machine

4
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:14,000
Before we start sewing the finished version, let's learn about the sewing machine tool set.

5
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:20,000
The sewing machine tool set can be found in 2D window or 3D window.

6
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:23,000
Their operation is different from each other.

7
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:29,000
First is the sewing machine tool. It can sew two separate lines together.

8
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:36,000
Use the sewing machine tool to click the first line, then move the mouse to the second line.

9
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:43,000
Before creating the sewing machine, please refer to the preview effect to make sure the direction is correct.

10
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:48,000
After confirming the direction is correct, click the second line and the sewing machine is completed.

11
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:53,000
The sewing machine tool is to identify the lines that are interrupted by a straight line.

12
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:59,000
Back to the previous step, now let's learn how to use the sewing machine tool in 3D window.

13
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:03,000
Click the first line, then click the second line.

14
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:09,000
The sewing machine tool in 3D and 2D window have no operation difference.

15
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:14,000
If our direction is the opposite, the sewing machine will cross.

16
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:19,000
At this time, we can switch to the editing sewing machine tool.

17
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:25,000
Go to the 2D or 3D window, click the right button on the wrong sewing machine and choose to change the sewing machine.

18
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:28,000
Now the sewing machine direction is correct.

19
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:37,000
If we want a more free sewing machine, please use the free sewing machine tool.

20
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:42,000
Click the right button, then move the mouse along the direction of the sewing machine.

21
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:46,000
Click again to finish the selection of the sewing line.

22
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:50,000
Then go to the second sewing machine and repeat the steps.

23
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:54,000
Click the right button, then move the mouse along the direction of the sewing machine.

24
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:56,000
At this time, there will be a blue dot.

25
00:01:56,000 --> 00:02:01,000
The blue dot shows the end point of the sewing line that is equal to the length of the first sewing line.

26
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:06,000
Click this blue dot to complete the creation of the long sewing line.

27
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:13,000
After learning the free sewing machine tool, we can try to edit the sewing line.

28
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:21,000
Use the edit sewing machine tool to drag the end point of the free sewing line to the straight line.

29
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:26,000
You can also drag the end point of the sewing line to the straight line.

30
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:29,000
You can also drag the end point of the sewing line to the other side of the sewing line.

31
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:34,000
When selecting the sewing line, click the right button and select delete sewing in the menu.

32
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:39,000
Or just press the delete button to delete the sewing line.

33
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:45,000
Now let's learn how to use the free sewing machine in the 3D window.

34
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:49,000
Switch to the free sewing machine and click on the 70 points.

35
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:52,000
Move the mouse in the direction of the sewing line to the end point of the first line.

36
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:55,000
Double-click the mouse to the left.

37
00:02:55,000 --> 00:03:00,000
Double-click is the end selection command for some of the common functions in the 3D window.

38
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:03,000
Then repeat the operation and click on the 70 points.

39
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:09,000
Then double-click on the end point to complete the creation of a set of sewing lines.

40
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:15,000
Of course, the free sewing machine can also use the straight line as the starting point or the end point.

41
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:17,000
Here we can see

42
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:22,000
that the end point of the free sewing machine can be the middle of a line.

43
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:28,000
And we can use the end point of other sewing lines to complete the sewing line.

44
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:36,000
Next, let's learn how to sew a line separated by multiple lines together.

45
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:39,000
I recommend you to create it in the 2D window.

46
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:41,000
Here we use the line sewing as an example.

47
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:45,000
Click on the first line in the same way as the previous operation.

48
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:47,000
Then press the Shift key.

49
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:50,000
At this time, the color of the sewing line will turn yellow-green.

50
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:53,000
It means that we are creating a 1 to n sewing line.

51
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:56,000
Then from left to right, the mouse is close to the left end point.

52
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:59,000
Click to select two lines.

53
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:03,000
After completion, release the Shift key and complete the creation.

54
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:07,000
Don't forget the sewing line in the middle.

55
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:13,000
Finally, the sewing line between the multiple lines and the multiple lines is created.

56
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:15,000
First, select the sewing line with the line sewing.

57
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:17,000
This is the same way of selecting the sewing line.

58
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:19,000
But we need to follow the order first.

59
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:23,000
Click on the good side of the line in the direction of the sewing line.

60
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:26,000
In the process of creating the sewing line,

61
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:31,000
if there is a mistake, you can press Backspace to return to the previous step.

62
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:33,000
After completing the selection of the good side,

63
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:36,000
press the Enter key to complete the selection confirmation.

64
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:40,000
After confirmation, the first set of sewing lines will turn pure green.

65
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:44,000
Then please press the sewing direction and order to select the second set of lines.

66
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:47,000
Press the Enter key again to complete the creation of the sewing line.

67
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:53,000
Finally, use the line sewing tool with the shortcut key N to create the sewing line between the panels.

68
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:59,000
Then select the top panel and press the right key to select the frozen panel in the candy window.

69
00:04:59,000 --> 00:05:03,000
The frozen panel will be fixed in the 3D space.

70
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:05,000
Press the control key to open the simulation.

71
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:09,000
You can see that the panel is properly sewn and becomes a pinstripe structure.

72
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:12,000
Go to the file in the upper left corner.

73
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:14,000
Go to the file in the upper left corner.

74
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:15,000
Open the project.

75
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:17,000
Open the previously saved file.

76
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:18,000
Select the line sewing tool.

77
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:22,000
In the 2D window, refer to the effect in the video to complete the sewing line.

78
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:24,000
First, the sewing line in the front of the panel.

79
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:28,000
Press the button to sew the two lines together.

80
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:31,000
Then continue to create the sewing line on the side of the panel.

81
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:34,000
Then the sewing line between the sleeves and the panel.

82
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:36,000
Note that the sewing line marks match.

83
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:40,000
You can also refer to the light blue preview sewing line effect in the 3D window.

84
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:41,000
Make sure there is no intersection.

85
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:43,000
Change the perspective.

86
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:46,000
Check which positions are not sewn.

87
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:52,000
Sew the sides of the sleeves together.

88
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:54,000
The golden line can be completed in the 3D window.

89
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:58,000
It is more convenient to match the sewing line direction.

90
00:05:58,000 --> 00:06:03,000
The front and sleeves are created by matching the panel, panel and sewing line.

91
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:06,000
The back panel itself is a panel with a left and right symmetry.

92
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:08,000
Since the panels are in a symmetrical state,

93
00:06:08,000 --> 00:06:11,000
you can see that the sewing line on the other side will be created automatically.

94
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:14,000
Next, let's create the sewing line of the pocket.

95
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:18,000
It is more convenient to use the free sewing tool here.

96
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:19,000
Click the starting point.

97
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:21,000
Move the mouse along the sewing direction.

98
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:23,000
Click the end point.

99
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:27,000
Then go to the inner line of the large body and perform the same operation.

100
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:32,000
Of course, we can also use the free sewing tool to sew in the 3D window.

101
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:37,000
Press the control key to return to the previous step of the operation.

102
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:39,000
The free sewing of the 2D window is a little different.

103
00:06:39,000 --> 00:06:42,000
Because there is a shorter edge in the pocket,

104
00:06:42,000 --> 00:06:46,000
it will automatically select the shorter edge.

105
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:49,000
Therefore, when we select the free sewing line,

106
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:52,000
we need to press and hold to confirm the direction of the sewing line.

107
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:54,000
Double-click to confirm the selection.

108
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:58,000
Adjust the angle to prevent the panel from blocking and affecting the selection of the sewing line.

109
00:06:58,000 --> 00:07:00,000
Similarly, click the starting point.

110
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:05,000
Move the mouse along the sewing line and press and hold to confirm the correct direction.

111
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:08,000
Finally, double-click to complete the creation of this pair of sewing lines.

112
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:12,000
After the sewing line is completed,

113
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:13,000
open the simulation.

114
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:16,000
Here I choose to use the GPU simulation.

115
00:07:16,000 --> 00:07:17,000
For the simulation quality,

116
00:07:17,000 --> 00:07:19,000
select the default normal speed.

117
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:21,000
After opening the simulation,

118
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:24,000
the clothing will be influenced by the gravity in the environment and the sewing line,

119
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:27,000
and will be worn on the virtual model.

120
00:07:29,000 --> 00:07:31,000
In addition to the manual creation of the sewing line,

121
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:33,000
for the simpler clothing structure,

122
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:36,000
we can use the automatic sewing function.

123
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:37,000
The automatic sewing function

124
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:42,000
will take into account the location and shape of each panel and create the sewing line.

125
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:45,000
First, change to the ice sewing line tool.

126
00:07:45,000 --> 00:07:48,000
Press Ctrl A to select all the sewing lines,

127
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:51,000
then press the Delete key to delete them.

128
00:07:51,000 --> 00:07:54,000
Since the pocket does not belong to the body structure part,

129
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:56,000
we can temporarily delete it first,

130
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:57,000
and then add it back.

131
00:07:57,000 --> 00:07:59,000
Then go to the 3D tool bar,

132
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:02,000
select all 3D arrangement positions.

133
00:08:02,000 --> 00:08:05,000
All panels will be arranged around the virtual model before the simulation.

134
00:08:05,000 --> 00:08:08,000
Then you can use the automatic sewing function.

135
00:08:11,000 --> 00:08:13,000
In the window display,

136
00:08:13,000 --> 00:08:15,000
select the type of clothing.

137
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:18,000
There are clothes, pants and dresses to choose from.

138
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:20,000
For the different clothing types,

139
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:22,000
the specific options for the bottom are also different.

140
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:26,000
The front gold is a closed-door closed-door type.

141
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:28,000
Here, select closed,

142
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:30,000
so that the front and middle will be all sewed together.

143
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:34,000
The front gold is a closed-door closed-door type.

144
00:08:35,000 --> 00:08:39,000
Since there is no collar, you can automatically select the shape of the collar.

145
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:43,000
Click to confirm that the seam line will be automatically created between the panels.

146
00:08:45,000 --> 00:08:49,000
Rotate the view to check if there is a missing seam line.

147
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:54,000
Then start the simulation, the clothes will be worn on the virtual model.

148
00:08:54,000 --> 00:09:02,000
Then switch to the adjustment panel tool, select the inner line of the entire pocket, click on the right, select the colon as the panel with the seam line.

149
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:10,000
After arranging the position between the 2D window and the 3D window separately, use the edit seam line tool to delete the excess seam line.

150
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:16,000
Select the seam line at the opening, click on the delete button to delete.

151
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:20,000
Press the control button to start the simulation, the pocket is done.

152
00:09:21,000 --> 00:09:26,000
This is the knowledge about sewing, see you in the next video.

